440	 * run because a stopped run rarely got a mention at all -- and the moment it did, it
441	 * was telling the person who had just stopped it that it had finished. "Review the
442	 * results" is dropped for the same reason: a run cut short may have none.
443	 *
444	 * `failed` gets its own sentence because "did not finish before it finished" is what
445	 * the cut-short wording would build from it, and because it is the one interrupted
446	 * ending whose text may be a fragment of ordinary work rather than a stop landing
447	 * between sentences.
